# Fork-owned files that upstream will never accept.
#
# This list is the secondary guardrail behind the merge-conflict abort
# in sync-upstream.yml: after a clean (non-conflicting) merge, the
# workflow verifies that every file below still exists on master and
# still contains its survival marker. If upstream silently dropped a
# fork-owned file in a clean merge, the sync fails and a `sync`-labeled
# issue is opened so a human can restore it.
#
# Each entry: <path>  ::  <survival-marker-string>
#
# When you add or change a fork-owned file:
#   1. Add the file to this list with a marker that is unique to the
#      fork's version (e.g. a slash command name, a config section
#      name, or a literal string the fork writes that upstream does
#      not). Verify the marker exists on master before committing.
#   2. After an upstream sync, run the workflow (or re-trigger it via
#      `workflow_dispatch`) to confirm all markers still resolve.
#
# Do not remove entries from this list unless the fork-owned feature
# has been intentionally retired and the corresponding upstream merge
# has removed the source code.

